{
  "id": "p10",
  "title": "Arrays",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "p10-l1",
      "title": "array[1..n] of",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "An array holds many values of the same type under one name: var score: array[1..5] of integer; Each element has an index: score[1] … score[5].",
        "In Pascal, you choose the range yourself. It doesn't have to start at 0 or 1: array[1983..1990] of integer works too.",
        "Turbo Pascal checks the index: score[6] in an array[1..5] stops the program with Runtime error 201: Range check error."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "program Scores;",
          "var",
          "  score: array[1..3] of integer;",
          "  sales: array[1983..1990] of integer;",
          "begin",
          "  score[1] := 72;",
          "  score[2] := 95;",
          "  score[3] := 88;",
          "  writeln('First: ', score[1]);",
          "  writeln('Sum: ', score[1] + score[2] + score[3]);",
          "  sales[1984] := 2;",
          "  sales[1985] := 7;",
          "  writeln('Sold in 1985: ', sales[1985]);",
          "end."
        ],
        "output": [
          "First: 72",
          "Sum: 255",
          "Sold in 1985: 7"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "p10-l1-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "How many elements does array[1..10] of integer have?",
          "options": [
            "10",
            "9",
            "11",
            "1"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Indexes 1 to 10."
        },
        {
          "id": "p10-l1-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does Turbo Pascal do with score[6] in an array[1..5]?",
          "options": [
            "Runtime error 201: Range check error",
            "It returns 0",
            "It uses score[5]",
            "It makes the array bigger"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "The index is checked."
        },
        {
          "id": "p10-l1-e3",
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "prompt": "Declare an array for 7 temperatures.",
          "code": [
            "var",
            "  temp: array[1___7] of real;"
          ],
          "options": [
            "..",
            ",",
            "-",
            " to "
          ],
          "answer": "..",
          "explanation": "A range is written with two dots."
        },
        {
          "id": "p10-l1-e4",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does this program print?",
          "code": [
            "program A;",
            "var",
            "  a: array[1..3] of integer;",
            "begin",
            "  a[1] := 5;",
            "  a[2] := 10;",
            "  a[3] := 20;",
            "  writeln(a[2] + a[3]);",
            "end."
          ],
          "options": [
            "30",
            "10",
            "20",
            "an error"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "a[2] + a[3] = 10 + 20."
        },
        {
          "id": "p10-l1-e5",
          "type": "find_bug",
          "prompt": "This program stops with a range check error. Which line is wrong?",
          "code": [
            "program Days;",
            "var",
            "  rain: array[1..7] of integer;",
            "begin",
            "  rain[1] := 3;",
            "  rain[7] := 0;",
            "  rain[8] := 5;",
            "end."
          ],
          "answer": 6,
          "explanation": "The array only goes from 1 to 7."
        },
        {
          "id": "p10-l1-e6",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "Can a Pascal array start at 1983?",
          "options": [
            "Yes, array[1983..1990] of … is fine",
            "No, arrays always start at 0",
            "No, arrays always start at 1",
            "Only for real numbers"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "You pick the index range that fits the data."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p10-l2",
      "title": "Loops over Arrays",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "A for loop goes through every element: for i := 1 to 5 do sum := sum + a[i]; That's where arrays shine.",
        "To pass an array to a procedure, give the array type a name first: type TList = array[1..5] of integer; Then procedure Show(a: TList);",
        "Use var for big arrays, even if you don't change them: then nothing has to be copied."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "program Loop;",
          "type",
          "  TList = array[1..5] of integer;",
          "var",
          "  list: TList;",
          "  i, sum: integer;",
          "",
          "procedure Show(var a: TList);",
          "var",
          "  i: integer;",
          "begin",
          "  for i := 1 to 5 do",
          "    write(a[i]:4);",
          "  writeln;",
          "end;",
          "",
          "begin",
          "  for i := 1 to 5 do",
          "    list[i] := i * i;",
          "  Show(list);",
          "  sum := 0;",
          "  for i := 1 to 5 do",
          "    sum := sum + list[i];",
          "  writeln('Sum: ', sum);",
          "end."
        ],
        "output": [
          "   1   4   9  16  25",
          "Sum: 55"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "p10-l2-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "How do you go through all elements of array[1..8]?",
          "options": [
            "for i := 1 to 8 do …",
            "for i := 0 to 8 do …",
            "while a do …",
            "for each a do …"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "From the first index to the last one."
        },
        {
          "id": "p10-l2-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "Why give an array type a name with type?",
          "options": [
            "So it can be used for parameters",
            "It makes the array faster",
            "Pascal needs it for every array",
            "To make it global"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "procedure Show(a: array[1..5] of integer) is not allowed; the type needs a name."
        },
        {
          "id": "p10-l2-e3",
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "prompt": "Declare a named array type.",
          "code": [
            "type",
            "  TDays ___ array[1..7] of integer;"
          ],
          "options": [
            "=",
            ":",
            ":=",
            "is"
          ],
          "answer": "=",
          "explanation": "Types are defined with =, like constants."
        },
        {
          "id": "p10-l2-e4",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does this program print?",
          "code": [
            "program D;",
            "var",
            "  a: array[1..3] of integer;",
            "  i: integer;",
            "begin",
            "  for i := 1 to 3 do",
            "    a[i] := i * 2;",
            "  for i := 1 to 3 do",
            "    write(a[i], ' ');",
            "  writeln;",
            "end."
          ],
          "options": [
            "2 4 6",
            "1 2 3",
            "2 4 6 8",
            "6"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Each element is i * 2."
        },
        {
          "id": "p10-l2-e5",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "Why pass a big array as var?",
          "options": [
            "So it isn't copied",
            "Because it must change",
            "It's required",
            "To make it smaller"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "A value parameter copies the whole array."
        },
        {
          "id": "p10-l2-e6",
          "type": "order_lines",
          "prompt": "Put the lines in order: add up all elements.",
          "lines": [
            "sum := 0;",
            "for i := 1 to 10 do",
            "  sum := sum + a[i];",
            "writeln(sum);"
          ],
          "answer": [
            "sum := 0;",
            "for i := 1 to 10 do",
            "  sum := sum + a[i];",
            "writeln(sum);"
          ],
          "explanation": "Start at 0, add each element, print at the end."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p10-l3",
      "title": "Two Dimensions",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "An array can have two indexes, like a table: var board: array[1..3, 1..3] of char; board[2, 3] is row 2, column 3.",
        "Two nested loops go through every cell.",
        "The index can also be a char: count: array['a'..'z'] of integer; gives one counter per letter."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "program Board;",
          "var",
          "  board: array[1..3, 1..3] of char;",
          "  r, c: integer;",
          "begin",
          "  for r := 1 to 3 do",
          "    for c := 1 to 3 do",
          "      board[r, c] := '.';",
          "  board[1, 1] := 'X';",
          "  board[2, 2] := 'O';",
          "  board[3, 1] := 'X';",
          "  for r := 1 to 3 do",
          "  begin",
          "    for c := 1 to 3 do",
          "      write(board[r, c], ' ');",
          "    writeln;",
          "  end;",
          "end."
        ],
        "output": [
          "X . . ",
          ". O . ",
          "X . . "
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "p10-l3-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "How many cells does array[1..4, 1..5] of integer have?",
          "options": [
            "20",
            "9",
            "45",
            "5"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "4 rows × 5 columns."
        },
        {
          "id": "p10-l3-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does grid[2, 3] mean?",
          "options": [
            "Row 2, column 3",
            "Row 3, column 2",
            "Element 2 to 3",
            "The 23rd element"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "First index, then second index."
        },
        {
          "id": "p10-l3-e3",
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "prompt": "Count the letter c.",
          "code": [
